  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 157 PM CDT Wed Jun 24 2026\n\nFor the long term, the forecast hasn't changed much over the past\n24 hours. An upper level trough is expected to move into the \nPacific Northwest late this week, and then into the northern U. S.\nRocky Mountain area by early next week. This will weaken the \nridging currently over the El Paso area shifting the upper level \nridging into the Ark-La-Miss region by Sunday. The ridge will \nexpand northward up the Mississippi and Ohio River Valleys by \nMonday. This pattern will put our western counties under southerly\nflow aloft, while the rest of the area remains under a ridge. \nCould see a few isolated showers or thunderstorms in our western \ncounties, but will leave the forecast generally dry for now.",
